; soak-prep: before the 30-minute soak on the drop-in (a fresh boot). Mounts
; and formats SBA: (FFS2) and SBB: (SFS) on unit 5, records the reference
; hashes and free memory, and clears the stop file. Then start three jobs
; at once:
;   Execute SHARED:sbench/soak-torture        (2 x 900 s, then the stop file)
;   Execute SHARED:sbench/soak-fs SBA ffs     (rounds until the stop file)
;   Execute SHARED:sbench/soak-fs SBB sfs
; and when all three are done: Execute SHARED:sbench/soak-end
FailAt 30
MakeDir SHARED:sbench/soak >NIL:
Delete SHARED:sbench/soak/#? QUIET FORCE >NIL:
Copy SHARED:sbench/vscsitest RAM: QUIET
Protect RAM:vscsitest +rwed QUIET
Mount SBA: FROM SHARED:sbench/sb.mountlist
Mount SBB: FROM SHARED:sbench/sb.mountlist
Echo "" >RAM:cr
SYS:System/Format <RAM:cr DRIVE SBA: NAME SoakFFS QUICK NOICONS
SYS:System/Format <RAM:cr DRIVE SBB: NAME SoakSFS QUICK NOICONS
CD SYS:Libs
C:MD5Sum #? >SHARED:sbench/soak/src.md5
CD RAM:
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Avail TOTAL >SHARED:sbench/soak/mem-start.txt
Date >SHARED:sbench/soak/start.txt
Echo "soak ready"
